  "content": {
    "title": "UMBC vs Howard March Madness time, streaming: \nWinner to play Michigan",
    "text": "Updated March 17, 2026, 5:18 p.m. ETEditor's note: Follow live updates from UMBC-Howard in the First Four of 2026 March Madness.Michigan basketball is ready to make a big-time tournament run, but its first opponent has yet to be decided.The First Four of the 2026 NCAA Tournament features a matchup between 16-seed UMBC and 16-seed Howard on Tuesday, March 17, at UD Arena in Dayton, Ohio. The game is scheduled for 6:40 p.m. ET and will be televised on truTV, with the winner advancing to play 1-seed Michigan on Thursday, March 19.That game will take place at KeyBank Center in Buffalo, New York, with tipoff scheduled for 7:10 p.m. ET (CBS).Watch NCAA Tournament on SlingUMBC finished first in the America East regular-season standings and won the conference tournament with a 74-59 win over Vermont on Saturday, March 14. With the win, the Retrievers earned the conference's automatic bid and will face Howard in the First Four for a chance to play in the first round.Howard, meanwhile, finished atop the MEAC with a 23-10 regular-season record and earned the conference's automatic bid by beating North Carolina Central, 70-63, in the MEAC Tournament final on Saturday. This is Howard's third NCAA Tournament appearance in the last four seasons.Though the Bisons have had more recent tournament appearances, UMBC has carved a place in NCAA tournament history as the first 16-seed to defeat a 1-seed when the Retrievers beat No. 1-seed Virginia, 74-54, in the 2018 NCAA Tournament. UMBC lost to Kansas State in its second-round matchup that year and has not been back to the tournament since.Here's what you need to know about Tuesday's First Four matchup.UMBC vs Howard time, March Madness First FourDate: Tuesday, March 17.Time: 6:40 p.m. ET.Location: UD Arena, Dayton.UMBC vs Howard channel, March Madness First FourTipoff: 6:40 p.m. ET.Channel: truTV.Streaming: Sling.Tuesday's First Four matchup between UMBC and Howard can be watched on truTV, with streaming available on Sling.Watch UMBC-Howard on SlingUMBC vs Howard prediction in First FourTony Garcia, Detroit Free Press: It's the battle of the DMV. Howard has a pair of capable guards in Bryce Harris and Cedric Taylor III who both average more than 17 points and nearly seven rebounds, yet the Bison also give the ball away on more non-steal turnovers than any other team in the country. UMBC meanwhile is No. 27 in the country in turnover rate (14.1%). The pick: UMBC 72, Howard 69.UMBC vs Howard odds, March Madness First FourSpread: UMBC: -1½ points (+104); Howard +1½ (-128).Over/under: 142½ points.Moneyline: UMBC (-106), Howard (-113).All odds are courtesy of FanDuel as of Tuesday morning.Need to catch up on the news during your lunch break? Sign up for our Sports Briefing newsletter to get daily summaries of Detroit sports! You can reach Christian at cromo@freepress.com.",
